# Foundation Uno — Vercel CLI upload exclusion (UNO-WO-012 / R02).
#
# Purpose: keep private authority, task scratch, credentials and build output OUT of a
# CLI-initiated upload of this repository.
#
# Scope and honest limits:
#   * This file is an ADDITIONAL layer for CLI uploads such as `vercel deploy` from a local
#     checkout. It is NOT proof of protection for a Git-imported Vercel project: a Git clone
#     contains exactly the tracked files of the commit, so `.gitignore` and the tracked set
#     govern what exists there, not this file.
#   * It must never screen the build inputs Vercel needs. `src/`, `next.config.ts`,
#     `package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `tsconfig.json` and `next-env.d.ts` stay eligible.
#   * An ignore list never deletes, moves or rewrites anything.

# --- Private Owner authority and project records ---------------------------
# The whole documents tree, including the private ACTIVE work order, is not an upload input.
.documents/

# --- Task scratch, local evidence and logs --------------------------------
.temp/
tmp/
*.log

# --- Version control and provider state -----------------------------------
.git/
.vercel/

# --- Credentials and environment ------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- Installed and generated Node / Next.js output ------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Coverage and tool caches ---------------------------------------------
coverage/
.eslintcache
.cache/
